{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good afternoon Mr Deshmukh. It has been six weeks since the hip operation, yes? How have you been getting on?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes doctor, six weeks yesterday, the right hip replacement. I have come for that check the surgeon insisted on, I did not want to miss the date. My daughter dropped me and she is waiting outside with the file.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right, so the routine six week review after the right hip replacement. You walked in with a stick, I saw that. How is the wound, any discharge or redness?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): No discharge and no redness. I was very particular, no water on it for two full weeks, then the clips came out. After that I kept it open to the air only.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): The scar looks healed, doctor. His daughter was saying the cut healed in five days. And uh she said he does not take the asprin on Sundays.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): The five days part is correct, it closed very fast, I was surprised only. But not Sunday, she always mixes the days. I skip the aspirin on Saturday, temple morning I take nothing and after lunch I forget, and Sunday I do take it.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): So the wound closed quickly, and the aspirin is missed on Saturday, not Sunday. What strength is the aspirin, and why was it started?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): It is 150 mg, one tablet after food, once a day. They gave it so that clots do not form after the hip operation. I have not stopped it, only that Saturday gap.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. You have high blood pressure from before, am I right?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, hypertension, twelve years now. Amlodipin 5 mg every morning, I never miss that one, even on Saturday. My physician started it in Pune and I brought the same tablets here.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, and the pressure just now, she told me one thirty eight over eighty four. I wrote it in my small diary, I keep every reading, and my daughter laughs at that diary.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Yes, that is the reading I took outside. Blood pressure 138 over 84, pulse 76, regular.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): 138 over 84, pulse 76. Any swelling of the calf since the operation, the back of the lower leg?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not at all. Every night I press both calves and my daughter looks also, there is no puffiness and the skin is the same on both sides.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good. With the blood pressure, do you get headaches?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, actually sometimes. Afternoon time, a dull headache, maybe twice in a week, I lie down and it goes. Not a big one.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): And giddiness along with that?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either. No spinning, no feeling of faint.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain, or shortness of breath when you walk?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Never. I can walk to the gate talking the whole way, no chest pain and no gasping.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the hip itself, is it painful now?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No, not really. The operation pain is finished. I am managing with the stick, slowly slowly.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok. What about the evenings, after you have been on your feet?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah well, actually if I am honest the right hip does ache in the evening. After I walk to the gate and back it is a dull ache, not in the morning. I cannot say when it started, maybe ten days or maybe two weeks, I did not write the date, and if I sit with the leg up it settles.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): For that ache I take paracetemol, err, 500 milligram I think, two tablets only when it comes. The strip at home is faded, so I am not sure of the strength.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me say it back. Wound healed with no discharge, no calf swelling, aspirin 150 mg once a day but left out on Saturdays, amlodipine 5 mg each morning for twelve years of hypertension, dull afternoon headache twice a week, no giddiness, no chest pain, no breathlessness. The evening right hip ache you cannot date, and paracetamol two tablets when it comes, strength not certain.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Correct, all of that. These days I am staying with my daughter, not alone, she cooks and I do not lift anything. The traffic was very bad, that is why we were a little late, sorry.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): I had a look just now. The scar on the right hip is dry and healed, no redness. Both calves are soft, the right calf is not swollen, and you are walking with one stick, which is fine at this stage.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think the evening ache is ordinary healing pain after the hip replacement. I cannot fully rule out a simple muscle strain, but this is not the picture of a clot.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Take the aspirin every day, Saturday included, once you are back from the temple. Use two paracetamol tablets when the ache comes, not more than three times in a day, and keep the stick for now.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): If the calf swells or the ache becomes much worse, come back sooner. Otherwise I will see you in six weeks. We might do a hip xray only if the ache has not settled by then. Any problem with passing urine?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No, urine is normal, no burning. Six weeks is fine, my daughter will bring me. Thank you doctor."
 ],
